Hi Erin,

Thanks for your comments on the guide. I have attached v1.0 with the contrasting passages we discussed on Tuesday. P02 shows how a reference to the relevant table and row can identify the fact even when the title is not copied; P04 gives us a useful contrast because the choice of room alone does not supply the capacity evidence.

For the next read, let's look separately for the check and for the action the writer actually gives if confirmation is missing. P06 asks for a check but does not state what happens without it; P15 does name two sittings. We should not add an action ourselves just because it seems sensible.

The April CSVs will remain as our independent readings, including the original scores. The annotated judgments are examples for the next marking, not replacements for those records. We'll keep the three criteria at four points each.

Thanks,
Heather

